<h1 style="color: #192147; font-weight: 800; font-size: 32px; line-height: 150%; margin-bottom: 32px;">
Fleet news: November 2026
</h1>
<p style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 24px; font-weight: 400; margin-bottom: 16px;">
Our first virtual summit streams free on November 10, and <a style="display: inline; color: #515774; cursor: pointer; text-decoration: underline; text-underline-offset: 4px; text-decoration-color: #C5C7D1; font-size: 16px; word-break: break-word;" href="https://www.linkedin.com/events/7518683538410459136/" target="_blank">you&#39;re invited</a>! October also brought two releases, including a heads-up for Mac users before Fleet patches the apps they&#39;re working in. Let&#39;s dig in!
</p>
<h2 style="color: #192147; font-weight: 700; font-size: 24px; line-height: 150%; margin-bottom: 24px; margin-top: 32px;">
🚀 What shipped last month
</h2>
<ul style="padding-left: 16px; margin-bottom: 32px;">
<li style="margin-bottom: 16px; color: #009A7D;"><span style="color: #515774;">
<strong style="display: inline; font-weight: 700; color: #192147">Warn end users before patching macOS apps.</strong> Patch policies can now notify end users when an open app is about to update. Fleet Desktop lists the apps, waits an hour with a reminder five minutes before, and then installs the update, so nobody loses unsaved work.
</span></li>
<li style="margin-bottom: 16px; color: #009A7D;"><span style="color: #515774;">
<strong style="display: inline; font-weight: 700; color: #192147">Zero-touch enrollment for company-owned Android.</strong> Ship company-owned Android devices straight to end users, and they enroll in Fleet the first time they&#39;re turned on. As of Fleet 4.94.0, you choose which fleet each device lands in.
</span></li>
<li style="margin-bottom: 16px; color: #009A7D;"><span style="color: #515774;">
<strong style="display: inline; font-weight: 700; color: #192147">Self-service configuration profiles for Mac.</strong> Offer configuration profiles that end users install themselves from the <strong style="display: inline; font-weight: 700; color: #192147">My device</strong> page.
</span></li>
</ul>
<p style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 24px; font-weight: 400; margin-bottom: 16px;">
Also new: a configuration profile editor, Windows local admin password rotation, on-demand FileVault key rotation, and reports that keep a result for every host instead of stopping at 1,000. <a style="display: inline; color: #515774; cursor: pointer; text-decoration: underline; text-underline-offset: 4px; text-decoration-color: #C5C7D1; font-size: 16px; word-break: break-word;" href="https://fleetdm.com/releases" target="_blank">See every release</a>.
</p>
<h2 style="color: #192147; font-weight: 700; font-size: 24px; line-height: 150%; margin-bottom: 24px; margin-top: 32px;">
🗺️ What we plan to ship this month
</h2>
<p style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 24px; font-weight: 400; margin-bottom: 16px;">
Fleet 4.95.0 is planned for November. These are planned, not promised, and scope changes as the release comes together.
</p>
<ul style="padding-left: 16px; margin-bottom: 32px;">
<li style="margin-bottom: 16px; color: #009A7D;"><span style="color: #515774;">
<strong style="display: inline; font-weight: 700; color: #192147">AI tools in software inventory.</strong> See which AI tools are installed across your hosts on the <strong style="display: inline; font-weight: 700; color: #192147">Software</strong> page, <strong style="display: inline; font-weight: 700; color: #192147">Host details</strong>, and <strong style="display: inline; font-weight: 700; color: #192147">My device</strong>, without writing a custom report.
</span></li>
<li style="margin-bottom: 16px; color: #009A7D;"><span style="color: #515774;">
<strong style="display: inline; font-weight: 700; color: #192147">Patch deadlines for macOS apps.</strong> Set a deadline for Fleet-maintained app patches, so updates land within your organization&#39;s patching rules.
</span></li>
<li style="margin-bottom: 16px; color: #009A7D;"><span style="color: #515774;">
<strong style="display: inline; font-weight: 700; color: #192147">Configuration profile validation.</strong> Fleet checks the type, keys, and values in Apple and Windows configuration profiles, so you know a profile built with Fleet&#39;s AI-native builder, or any other tool, is valid before it reaches a host.
</span></li>
</ul>
<p style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 24px; font-weight: 400; margin-bottom: 16px;">
Also on deck: Okta conditional access for Windows hosts, scoping Android Play Store apps with labels, running a bootstrap package during manual macOS enrollment, and multiple versions of the same App Store app for iOS, iPadOS, and Android.
</p>
<p style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 24px; font-weight: 400; margin-bottom: 16px;">
Fleet plans releases in the open. The <a style="display: inline; color: #515774; cursor: pointer; text-decoration: underline; text-underline-offset: 4px; text-decoration-color: #C5C7D1; font-size: 16px; word-break: break-word;" href="https://github.com/orgs/fleetdm/projects/87/views/10" target="_blank">release planning board</a> shows what&#39;s queued for the releases after this one, and the <a style="display: inline; color: #515774; cursor: pointer; text-decoration: underline; text-underline-offset: 4px; text-decoration-color: #C5C7D1; font-size: 16px; word-break: break-word;" href="https://fleetdm.com/announcements/roadmap-preview-october-2026" target="_blank">October roadmap preview</a> walks through the next 90 days, including Fleet 5.
</p>
